---
import Solution from '../../layouts/Solution.astro';
import SolutionExample from '../../components/SolutionExample.astro';
import SolutionFit from '../../components/SolutionFit.astro';
import SolutionFaq from '../../components/SolutionFaq.astro';
import DocsHandoff from '../../components/DocsHandoff.astro';
import { solutionAreas } from '../../data/solutions';
import { describeServiceHref, contactEmail } from '../../data/contact';
const area = solutionAreas.find((a) => a.key === 'verifiable-credentials')!;
---
<Solution
  area={area}
  heading="Issue verifiable credentials from your register."
  description="Give people a digital credential stating information from your register, such as a professional licence’s recorded status. Its digital signature lets a receiving service check who issued it and whether it was altered. An implementation connects your register, a compatible digital wallet and the service that will accept the credential."
>
  <SolutionExample
    eyebrow="Illustrative licensing example"
    heading="Provide licence status without the licence history."
    intro="An employer needs to check a professional’s licence status. The professional council can issue a credential with that answer, without including the full licence record."
    items={[
      { term: 'The council issues', body: 'Evidence Gateway checks the council’s register and signs a credential containing the licence status. The dates show when the check was made and when the credential expires, not when the source record was last updated. The council authorizes which service may start issuance; the implementation controls how the offer reaches the intended person.' },
      { term: 'The professional receives', body: 'A separate delivery adapter sends the credential to a compatible digital wallet. The implementation team selects and tests the wallet, including how the person receives, stores and presents the credential.' },
      { term: 'The employer checks', body: 'The receiving service checks the issuer’s signature and the credential’s validity, then applies its own acceptance rules. The implementation connects this service and tests how it requests, verifies and accepts the credential.' },
    ]}
  />
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="credential-value-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What you can issue</p>
        <h2 id="credential-value-title">Choose the information each credential contains.</h2>
        <p>Your institution defines the question, the source information and the answer the credential may contain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="product-facts">
        <article><h3>Professional licence status</h3><p>State whether the register records a licence as current without including the licence number, exact expiry date or history of earlier decisions.</p></article>
        <article><h3>An age requirement</h3><p>State whether someone meets an age requirement without including their name or date of birth.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Programme enrollment</h3><p>An implementation can configure a credential to state whether someone is enrolled in a programme, without including the household’s assessment file.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <SolutionFit
    area={area}
    heading="Connect issuance, the wallet and the receiving service."
    muted
    jobs={{
      'evidence-gateway': 'Checks the agreed question against your data source and signs a credential containing the permitted answer.',
    }}
    extra={[
      { term: 'Credential delivery', body: 'A separate delivery adapter passes the credential to a compatible wallet. Your existing register can remain the source of information.' },
      { term: 'Wallet and receiving service', body: 'The implementation includes selecting and testing the wallet and connecting the receiving service. Registry Stack supplies verification tools; the service still needs to request and accept the credential, check its use and apply its own decision rules.' },
      { term: 'Issuance and operating arrangements', body: 'Agree how people request credentials, how access is checked, who hosts each part and how credentials are reissued when needed. These arrangements form part of the implementation scope.' },
    ]}
  >
    <p>Start with one credential and one receiving service. Test the complete journey from requesting the credential to using it.</p>
  </SolutionFit>
  <SolutionFaq
    items={[
      {
        q: 'Does Registry Stack include a digital wallet?',
        a: 'No. It supplies credential issuance, a delivery adapter and verification tools. We can help your team evaluate a wallet and receiving service for the implementation. Compatibility must be tested across receipt, storage and presentation.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What happens when the register changes?',
        a: 'An issued credential does not update automatically. The current software does not provide credential revocation or a status list. Your institution must set an appropriate validity period and agree how people obtain a fresh credential. A service that needs a current answer can make a new check against the register.',
        link: { href: '/solutions/check-a-fact/', label: 'Check information from another register' },
      },
      {
        q: 'What does verification establish?',
        a: 'Verification checks the issuer’s signature, the credential’s validity and proof that the presenting wallet controls the key linked to the credential. This does not by itself identify the person, prove the source record is correct or establish a legal entitlement. The receiving service must also check that the presentation is intended for this request and cannot be reused.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Can we use our existing register?',
        a: 'Yes. Your technical team can connect Evidence Gateway to your existing register or a read-only extract. The implementation must account for how recent that information is when issuing the credential.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Where can our technical team check the supported standards?',
        a: 'The documentation describes the supported SD-JWT VC credential format and the OpenID for Verifiable Credential Issuance (OID4VCI) profile. It also explains the delivery adapter and the work needed to integrate a wallet and verifier.',
        link: { href: 'https://docs.registrystack.org/configure/evidence-oid4vci/', label: 'Read the credential delivery guide' },
      },
    ]}
  />
  <DocsHandoff
    eyebrow="Work with us"
    heading="Discuss a credential your institution could issue."
    body="Tell us what the credential should state, who will receive it and which service will accept it. We can help define an implementation and evaluate the wallet and verification journey."
    primaryLabel="Discuss your service"
    primaryHref={describeServiceHref(area.name)}
    emphasis="docs"
    note={`Or write to ${contactEmail}.`}
  />
</Solution>
